      "message": "Thanks, agreed. PS2 replaces all remaining assertNotEqual port/ICMP-ID checks in this file with BIB checks. The helper now checks protocol and the inside/outside address/port tuple, including the pg2 VRF and pg3 one-armed cases. Static mappings still have their exact-port assertions.\n\nNine affected VPP tests pass on the existing local ARM64 Release build, seed 42, no retries: dynamic, hairpinning, ICMP error, prefixes, one-armed, static and the three fragment tests. Black and commit checks pass. A full-class attempt hit an abort in test_icmp_error_unsupported_inner_protocol on that older binary, so I am not claiming the complete class passed; fresh-build coverage is left to Gerrit CI.\n\nI also checked the seed: nat64_init clears the main structure and I found no initialization of random_seed before its use in nat64_random_port. I agree this needs a separate production follow-up. Seeding the existing PRNG would avoid the identical startup sequence; whether stronger port unpredictability is required deserves separate consideration.",
